#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:50
msgid "What we record and why"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:52
msgid "When you accept our Terms & Conditions we record that acceptance so that both you and we can later establish which version of the terms was agreed, and when. This is an access-control and contractual-compliance record. It is not marketing profiling and it is not used to make automated decisions about you."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:54
msgid "Legal basis"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:56
msgid "We rely on Article 6(1)(b) GDPR, because accepting the terms is necessary for the performance of the contract with you and for providing you access to the platform, and on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, our legitimate interests in the security of the platform, in accountability, and in being able to demonstrate and defend what was agreed. We do not rely on consent (Article 6(1)(a)) for this processing, so you are not asked to consent and cannot withdraw consent to it; you can instead object on the grounds described below."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:58
msgid "Data recorded for each acceptance"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:60
msgid "Your user account identifier, and your username and email address as they stood at that moment; the date and time in UTC together with the local time and time zone shown to you; the identifier, number and effective date of the version accepted; the action taken; the site the acceptance was made on; your IP address; and your browser identification (User-Agent). We do not use device fingerprinting and we do not collect MAC addresses or location data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:62
msgid "Who else receives it"
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyContent.php:64
